argument_evidence.context_text:
[7] The Officer’s Global Case Management System [GCMS] notes raised the following concerns:
The “high cost of international study in Canada when weighed against the potential career/employment benefits after completion”;
The “local options available for similar studies”;
The “Applicant had initially applied to one program and was refused” and “[h]as now applied to different programs and/or different institutions”;
The “[e]ducational goals in Canada are not consistent from one application to another with no explanation provided”; and
“One years tuition not paid in full”.

